<h2>NEW GDPR DIRECTIVE 25.05.2018 Data Protection Measures</h2>

<p>At cloudon.gr you can be sure and feel safe about your personal data. Some of the procedures we follow are the following:

<br>– Your account is accessed through a secure interface with our site to protect your data.

<br>– The backup copies are placed outside the Servers that serve your websites or your applications

<br>– Backups are encrypted with special algorithms

<br>– Access to all physical locations of the Datacenters is restricted to employees of our company or
of our partners and are monitored 24/7 via CCTV.

<br>– Only a very small number of employees have access to your data as well as that of your customers (mainly for support purposes) where absolutely necessary.

<br>– All employees have signed special non-disclosure agreements (NDAs) and have received mandatory security awareness training and the protection of your personal data.</p>

<h2>DataCenter Security</h2>

<p>Our Datacenters are controlled by all relevant bodies to achieve ISO 27001, PCI DSS, etc. certifications, which assure you that the infrastructure, your data handling and security meet the highest standards.</p >

<h2>Our Datacenters are based in the EU</h2>

<p>One of the conditions of the GDPR is that the storage of European citizens' data must be done within Europe. For this reason, all the Datacenters we cooperate with for the maintenance and storage of your personal data are based in Europe.</p>

<h2>Partners & “CloudON”</h2>

<p>For the sole purpose of the smooth operation of our company's electronic systems and IT infrastructure, we share the minimum required volumes of data with our partners. All third parties we work with have been carefully vetted for GDPR compliance.

<br>All of them have all the necessary certifications and standards to protect users' privacy.</p>

<h2>We hear your complaints & concerns</h2>

<p>If you have a question about data privacy, you should contact the DPO

<br>What is the DPO?
<br>According to the GDPR, we have designated a person to oversee all processes related to your data protection. This person is designated as a “data protection officer”

<br>Contact the data protection officer via E-mail: privacy@cloudon.gr and by phone at 210 2241 998 or by sending mail to the company's address which is: Mesogeion 460 & Paradisou 1 P.K.: 15342 Agia Paraskevi</ p>

